        "path": "/docs/accounting.txt",
        "content": "Case size: 6. Warehouse capacity: 180 units, including pending orders.\nOperating fee: 30 cents per simulated day. Shelf life: 6 days after arrival.\nPayment and invoice occur when an order is placed; the warehouse records a separate physical receipt on delivery.\nAn invoice is a claim on goods in transit and does not make goods available for sale.\nA batch is sellable on its arrival day through arrival_day + shelf_life, inclusive.\nFor each newly advanced day: receive deliveries, remove expired stock, sell FIFO, then pay the operating fee.\nDemand depends on the currently set selling price. Missed demand is lost, never backlogged.\nOrders debit all item and shipping costs immediately. Invalid operations never change world state.\nNo terminal inventory valuation, refunds, loans, or liquidation. Remaining stock and orders are worth zero for scoring.\nA cash shortage pays the available balance and records unpaid operating fees; any unpaid fee fails strict success.\n",
        "event_id": "e0001",
        "cost_used": 1
